it's Mother's Day tomorrow so it seemed  like a good reason as any to finally  talk about this this is a topic I have  been meaning to talk about for about as  long as I've been doing the animation  junkie sub series and I just never got  around it I kind of wish I had sooner  because it's I'm not sure it's as  relevant as it was my thought was first  thing I'm talking about it because  Disney seems to have kind of broken this  streak a little bit with their more  recent films or at least some of them  but it has been observed for a fairly  decent chunk of time now that there are  not a heck of a lot of mothers in Disney  movies for the main characters I'm  talking about a lot of well frequently  dead or had the very least absent  mothers often without explanation  leaving us to presume them to be dead  now to be fair there's actually there's  a lot of just flat-out orphan characters  leaving a lot of Disney movies which  means you know no mother or father but  there's a fair number of characters who  have a father present but no mother you  know you've got Ariel  you've got jasmine you've got Belle  you've got Bambi so you've got all these  characters who have a father but no  mother in addition to all the ones who  just have no parents at all so what does  Disney have against mothers nothing even  when you factor in how many you know  evil stepmother figures there are which  actually is not as many as you would  think at the first place but it's not a  campaign against mothers it's actually  in a kind of awkward way a praising of  mothers because the reason that mothers  are absent from so many of these stories  is not because Disney or any storyteller  honestly but Disney's just sort of the  the Disney animated films just where  I've seen it pointed out  the most they're not trying to say you  know mothers aren't good or we don't  need them it's not anything like that  I've seen people twisted into you know  the sort of what does Disney have  against mothers nothing Disney in a  basically kind of reverse psychology way  is saying how important mothers are  because really think about why they  aren't there the thing is is that  mothers especially and like I said this  happens less in the more recent movies  but especially in films from you know 20  years ago plus mothers were seen as the  stabilizing force within a family so no  mother  is immediate shorthand for this family  dynamic is broken because and actually  if anything it's often an indictment of  the fathers I mean look at some of the  father figures I mentioned going all the  way back to somebody like Bambi you have  this absentee not particularly emotional  very stern father figure the Disney  Renaissance words that seem to really  happen a lot you've got characters like  Triton who just doesn't really get his  daughter at all  you've got Maurice who's you know a nice  enough guy but is obviously not quite  all there and he's he can barely sort of  keep himself together  you've got the Sultan who is just a  bumbling fool and even in in stories  where the mothers are present but like  barely getting any emphasis something  like Sleeping Beauty you've got these  father's just being all this over the  top and and causing all these problems  because the mothers are seen as the  stabilizing centering force so by  minimizing them it is a quick and easy  way to explain without having to devote  a ton of screen time to it why this  family dynamic has problems and  obviously you remove both parents that's  even easier of course this this hero or  heroine  as some sort of you know issues in terms  of trust stability home life what have  you they have no parents but even if you  just remove if you're gonna remove one  and say that it's a destabilizing force  you're gonna remove the mother there's  very it's very rare in these animated  films that you end up with a single  mother because the societal cliche  expectation is that oh a woman can  handle that and that is me talking about  societal baggage societal stereotype the  stereotypes which are of course not  representative reality there's plenty of  fathers who are perfectly capable of  taking care of their kids there are  plenty of mothers who are in over their  heads it goes it runs the gamut there  are plenty of orphans who are perfectly  well-adjusted but in terms of our  cultural laws Moses in our cultural  understanding the baseline shorthand of  these stories is orphan really messed up  single father we're kind of on shaky  ground single mother you're probably  doing okay both parents fine kids fine  so anytime and that's not to say that  you can't have you know a character on a  journey of personal growth with some  damage with some issues going on evil  with too stable parents but you have to  really dig in and devote time to  explaining what that issue is and why  the parents can't help and if you're  making a film especially a film for kids  which tend to favor shorter run times  ninety minutes or even less sometimes  then you don't want to sink five seven  ten minutes into having to explain why  the problem the hero is having is  something that the parents can't help  with when you can just save a craft out  of time by removing one or both the  parents and like I said if you got to  remove just one remove the mother people  can people click much easier on the idea  of father being in over his head trying  to raise his kids for some reason we're  still fixated on the mister  mom thing and as outdated of thinking as  that is sometimes the pop culture  understanding of something takes a long  friggin time to catch up to the reality  that we all know when we stop and think  about it for more than a few seconds so  the the lack of mothers in Disney films  it's not an agenda it's not any  statement well it's not any intentional  negative statement on mothers or that  mothers aren't necessary if anything  it's frequently pointing out how much of  a hole is left when they are there and  how home how often fathers are in over  their heads so it's if you're gonna say  it's a condemnation of anything it's a  condemnation of fathers and actually I  remember I don't know if it's still the  case now cuz I I don't I don't watch as  much TV as I used to but I remember  we're in the early 2000s ish that it  really seemed to be a spate of  incredibly stupid fathers on television  I don't know what was up with that I  don't have any where I'm going with that  I'm just remembering that all of a  sudden I don't know if that's still a  thing but in any case I've been meaning  to give my thoughts out on there as to  why Disney tends to not have mothers and  their films it's because mothers are  important so happy Mother's Day whatever  your thoughts are on this or if you just  want to say why your mother is  particularly awesome drop something down  in the comments let's talk about it  there's all the stuff to do such as  support me on patreon like subscribe  deck Dedic then it did that leaks for  all that and more is down in the  description so until next time  this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

